            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "\r\n  `ts_tree_cursor_goto_first_child_for_point()` also returns the direct\r\n  child index. Would it be useful for `iter_children()` to expose this as\r\n  an optional third iterator value?\r\n\r\n  ```lua\r\n  for child, field, index in node:iter_children({ start = { row, col } }) do\r\n  end\r\n```\r\n  Existing two-value loops would ignore the additional value, and callers\r\n  would not need to search for the index of the child returned by the\r\n  positioned iterator.",
