            "body": "Sorry I didn't use draft before, I press the button `ready for review` by mistake. I think this pr still need to design. \r\n\r\nNow we have 2 questions: \r\n1. If we should return index addtionally, iee, return `node,field,index` in `iter_children`.\r\n2. If we should use cursor for old api `iter_children(nil)`. This will be faster for flat trees, but may be slower with small trees, or only consume few nodes. \r\n\r\nFor the second question, maybe we can use new api for child more than 16, and keep old api for child less than 16. But still when the iter only consume few nodes, like\r\n```lua\r\nfor node,field in parent:iter_children() do\r\nbreak\r\nend\r\n```\r\nwill be slower because the construction. ",
